[2022-03-31T10:50:54.000+0000 | Aleksey Midenkov]
{quote}The InnoDB dict_table_t actually corresponds to TABLE_SHARE in the SQL layer and not TABLE. The TABLE is a table handle or a cursor, which would roughly correspond to row_prebuilt_t in InnoDB.{quote}

You right. Moreover lifetimes of TABLE_SHARE and dict_table_t are independent by design. So we have to acquire TABLE_SHARE each time we need it in InnoDB.

